00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:09.450
Your next question comes from the line of Graham Parry from Citigroup.

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:10.570
Please go ahead.

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:16.570
Great. Thanks for taking my questions. So on telecast and a quick follow-up, as you just

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:22.290
issued, clarifies that 13 to 15% is what the trial is minimally powered to detect. I think you said

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:27.890
it was just what it was powered for, but I think the design paper says it's 20% on all comers.

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:33.890
And would you view that 13 to 15% as a clinically meaningful result? So that was a follow-up.

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:39.330
And then on REMI-MS, could you just comment on your confidence in achieving disability progression?

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:44.650
I was taught to the brain penetration of the molecule and action at the microglia compared

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:49.970
to remibrutinib, which actually didn't show that with statistical significance in its

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:50.970
phase three. Thank you.

00:00:50.970 --> 00:00:56.390
Yeah, thanks, Rob. So you are correct. 13 to 15 would mean a win. It's powered for

00:00:56.390 --> 00:01:03.570
20% for the patients who are 70 milligrams in DL and above, or 25% for the 90 milligram

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:09.570
DL and above. And so I think we would say in the mid-teens, it's clinically meaningful,

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:16.770
given that these patients have no other option, and that this is an independent risk factor.

00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:24.010
And so, yeah, we'll ultimately see what the data shows. And then with respect to REMI-MS,

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:29.610
I think we have everything that indicates to us that the trial has been conducted and

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:35.270
the data that we're seeing, that from an ARR standpoint, that we're on track versus

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:39.550
what we would have expected in the data set. As you know, with disability progression,

00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:46.490
we have no way to know. And I think it's very difficult for me to handicap that. We

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:52.810
saw the data with remibrutinib. We do believe that our molecule is more potent on the target

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:58.830
and more selective. And so we're hopeful that that leads to the improvements in disability

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:04.410
progression that would bring us in line with the antibody-based B-cell therapies. But

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:09.550
there's no way for us to assess that in any sort of objective way at this point until

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:10.550
we study with that.

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:12.990
Thank you.

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:13.990
Thank you.

